## (anonymous) (body-1)

Starts target listening, registers a local HTTP handler and a NETWORK_EVENT wait before sending POST data. It checks a truthy channel id, resource id equality, method, header and body, then destroys commands.

- reads: CommandsFactory; HTTP server; NETWORK_EVENT resource; captured request
- writes: Tab, local server, target/resource listeners, outgoing POST
- branches: The expected request is a single POST with fixed header/body/cause.
- result: Task completes after both observed paths and command cleanup.
- errors: Assertion failures/rejections abort; normal-path commands cleanup only.
- async: Waits independently for remote actor reply, resource and local server request.
- ownership: Server cleanup is registered by shared helper; commands destroyed explicitly.

